<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch Revolt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Revolt was the uprising of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> against Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule that began in the 1560s and led to the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a>. It drained the resources of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, and because Portugal was united with the Spanish crown from 1580 to 1640, Portuguese overseas possessions became targets of Dutch attack, weakening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt.jpg" alt="Dutch Revolt" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cornelis Claesz van Wieringen / Formerly attributed to Hendrick Cornelisz Vroom · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Gibraltar_1607.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
